{"decision":"edit","issues":[{"quote":"The dark backdrop and the line of circles persist throughout the excerpt","problem":"The visible row of circles is not constant throughout; some circles change hue, some enter or leave the view, and the white pair moves out of frame."},{"quote":"As the water passes over a circle it stretches into a hollow ring rather than a solid disc.","problem":"This overgeneralizes the distortion. Some lights become ring-like, but many circles remain solid discs."},{"quote":"The coloured dots hold their horizontal positions but cycle in hue","problem":"This is too absolute because the visible set of dots changes; only the fixed dots maintain their positions while hue changes occur."},{"quote":"until they leave the row","problem":"The white blobs move out of the frame/view; saying they leave the row implies the row is a track they exit, which is not directly visible."}],"caption":"The video captures a night scene viewed through a glass pane streaked with running water and scattered small droplets. Against the black background, a roughly horizontal row of out-of-focus coloured lights forms soft bokeh circles in red, amber, white and bright green. The dark backdrop and the row remain visible throughout, while the water on the pane keeps flowing, merging and reshaping in front of them, constantly changing their outlines.

Thin vertical rivulets and droplets continuously appear, merge and slide downward, warping the lights where they cross. Distortion sometimes turns a circle into a ring-like shape, though many circles stay solid. The fixed coloured dots hold their horizontal positions but cycle in hue, an amber light turning red and a red light later flashing back to yellow.

Meanwhile the two white bokeh blobs drift steadily leftward across the frame, sliding past the otherwise fixed coloured dots until they move out of view. The remaining coloured lights continue to glow and shift behind the running water.","length_note":""}
